{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wk57zSdHoTS4bC4QrajkmS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan-writer brief\n2\t\n3\tRead this only when delegating plan authoring. Copy everything inside the fence\n4\tinto a file, replacing every `«...»` placeholder, and send it with\n5\t`delegate run --model grok-4.7-xhigh --capability read-only < brief.md` (`read-write` only\n6\twhen the plan must land in the repo). Answer a `NEEDS_CONTEXT` job with `delegate resume`.\n7\t\n8\tA filled brief replaces placeholders and nothing else. `«PLAN_OUTPUT_PATH»`\n9\tbecomes `docs/plans/2026-07-09-delegate-skill.md`; `«Feature Name»` becomes the\n10\tfeature; `«PASTE_APPROVED_SPEC_OR_SUMMARY»` becomes the spec text or the paths to\n11\tpaste from. Sections whose shape the delegate should reuse rather than restate\n12\t(`Task structure`, `No placeholders`) can collapse to one line pointing back at\n13\tthis template.\n14\t\n15\t```text\n16\tYou are a plan-writing delegate. The orchestrator (a different model) already\n17\tbrainstormed and approved the design. Your job is to write ONE detailed\n18\timplementation plan markdown file — planning document only.\n19\t\n20\t## Hard rules\n21\t\n22\t- Do not delegate further.\n23\t- Do NOT implement code. Do NOT modify source. Do NOT run build/test commands\n24\t  except read-only inspection needed to name exact paths (`ls`, `rg`, `Read`).\n25\t- Do NOT commit. Do NOT create git commits or PRs.\n26\t- Your only deliverable is the plan content (and, if the orchestrator asked you\n27\t  to write a file, that single markdown path).\n28\t- If you lack a fact that blocks a correct plan (missing path, unclear API,\n29\t  ambiguous requirement), stop and ask. End your message with the question as\n30\t  the body and a trailing line exactly:\n31\t\n32\t  STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\n33\t\n34\t  The orchestrator will answer with `delegate resume` and you will continue. Do not\n35\t  guess through blockers.\n36\t- When the plan is complete, end with:\n37\t\n38\t  STATUS: DONE\n39\t\n40\t## Output path"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1dfab1ce-6a5b-4c5a-bcd2-82d221557b95","uuid":"deff57da-c23d-4bd9-aff0-5db0e8ece722","timestamp":"2026-10-01T11:19:38.359Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/user/work/delegate-14-skill/skills/delegate/plan-writer-brief.md","content":"# Plan-writer brief\n\nRead this only when delegating plan authoring. Copy everything inside the fence\ninto a file, replacing every `«...»` placeholder, and send it with\n`delegate run --model grok-4.7-xhigh --capability read-only < brief.md` (`read-write` only\nwhen the plan must land in the repo). Answer a `NEEDS_CONTEXT` job with `delegate resume`.\n\nA filled brief replaces placeholders and nothing else. `«PLAN_OUTPUT_PATH»`\nbecomes `docs/plans/2026-07-09-delegate-skill.md`; `«Feature Name»` becomes the\nfeature; `«PASTE_APPROVED_SPEC_OR_SUMMARY»` becomes the spec text or the paths to\npaste from. Sections whose shape the delegate should reuse rather than restate\n(`Task structure`, `No placeholders`) can collapse to one line pointing back at\nthis template.\n\n```text\nYou are a plan-writing delegate. The orchestrator (a different model) already\nbrainstormed and approved the design. Your job is to write ONE detailed\nimplementation plan markdown file — planning document only.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- Do not delegate further.\n- Do NOT implement code. Do NOT modify source. Do NOT run build/test commands\n  except read-only inspection needed to name exact paths (`ls`, `rg`, `Read`).\n- Do NOT commit. Do NOT create git commits or PRs.\n- Your only deliverable is the plan content (and, if the orchestrator asked you\n  to write a file, that single markdown path).\n- If you lack a fact that blocks a correct plan (missing path, unclear API,\n  ambiguous requirement), stop and ask. End your message with the question as\n  the body and a trailing line exactly:\n\n  STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\n  The orchestrator will answer with `delegate resume` and you will continue. Do not\n  guess through blockers.\n- When the plan is complete, end with:\n\n  STATUS: DONE\n\n## Output path","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":126}}}
